From 2b71882a72327daf1da2c44215dd074175c692a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:02:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] installd: PlaitOS app data backup streams

For PlaitOS's plait_backup service in system_server (Plait Backup, the
app with Android-DataBackup's UI): stream an app's data out as
zstd-compressed tar and restore it back, with the privileges installd
already has for rollback snapshots, so no new SELinux domain or
app_data_file access for anything else.

- plaitBackupAppData: CE, DE, Android/data, obb or media of a package,
  as entries "<pkg>/..." (Android-DataBackup's layout), cache and
  code_cache left out, sockets/fifos/devices never included.
- plaitRestoreAppData: replaces that data with an archive's. Every path
  is walked one component at a time with openat + O_NOFOLLOW, entries
  outside "<pkg>/", "..", absolute paths, hard links and devices are
  refused or skipped, and everything is owned by the app (the tar's
  owners are ignored), permission bits only. Labels are reset with
  restorecon (per-app categories for CE/DE). Only app uids.
- plaitBackupApks: the *.apk files of a code dir under /data/app.
- plaitZstdDecompress: for APK archives, which system_server unpacks.

All calls are system_server only (ENFORCE_UID(AID_SYSTEM)) and hold
the package lock. SIGPIPE is blocked on the calling thread while
streaming, so a reader that goes away is an error, not a crash.

